;; John 1. Format: gsb/translation/README.md. Check: make gsb/lint

(note "**Opening (1:1-5).** The prologue answers Genesis 1:1 LXX: both begin ἐν ἀρχῇ, and both are rendered \"In [the] beginning\" with the same concordance gloss, so the echo is visible in English as it is in Greek.")

(note "**ἦν against ἐγένετο.** Verses 1-2 say what the Word *was* (ἦν, imperfect of εἰμί); verse 3 says what *came to be* (ἐγένετο, aorist of γίνομαι). The literal layer keeps the two verbs apart everywhere (\"was\" / \"came to be\") rather than using \"was made\", which would hide the contrast and add a passive the Greek does not have.")

(note "**Punctuation of 1:3-4.** Nestle 1904 puts the period after ὃ γέγονεν (\"... not even one [thing] which has come to be. In him life was\"). Many editions put it before ὃ γέγονεν (\"... not even one [thing]. What has come to be in him was life\"). We follow our base text's punctuation; the other division is a live option and is noted here, not adopted.")

